  "interpretation": "<p>Bile salt and bile pigment in urine indicates liver disorders. Bile pigment may pass into the blood and then in to the urine in certain liver&nbsp;diseases, anemia and infections. Bile salt and bile pigment in urine indicate hyperbilirubinemia. These are usually seen in obstructive&nbsp;jaundice and in less quantity in hepatocellular jaundice.</p>",
